<title>UK: SOCCER-EUROPEAN CUP WINNERS' CUP 2ND ROUND, 2ND LEG RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-EUROPEAN CUP WINNERS' CUP 2ND ROUND, 2ND LEG RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of second round, second</p>
<p>leg matches in the European Cup Winners' Cup on Thursday:</p>
<p>In Stockholm: AIK Stockholm (Sweden) 0 Nimes (France) 1</p>
<p>(halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Michael Brundin (own goal, 69)</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,620</p>
<p>AIK win 3-2 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Moscow: Lokomotiv Moscow (Russia) 2 Benfica (Portugal) 3</p>
<p>(1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Lokomotiv - Andrei Solomatin (9), Oleg Garas (58)</p>
<p>Benfica - Nicu Panduru (47), Osmar Candido (63) Joao Pinto</p>
<p>(90)</p>
<p>Attendance: 7,000</p>
<p>Benfica win 4-2 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Belgrade: Red Star Belgrade (Yugoslavia) 1 Barcelona (Spain) 1 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Red Star - Zoran Jovicic (47)</p>
<p>Barcelona - Giovanni Silva (48)</p>
<p>Attendance: 50,000</p>
<p>Barcelona win 4-2 on aggregate  </p>
<p>In Liverpool: Liverpool (England) 6 Sion (Switzerland) 3 (1-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Liverpool - Steve McManaman (28), Stig Inge Bjornebye (54), John Barnes (65), Robbie Fowler (70, 71), Patrick Berger (89)</p>
<p>Sion - Frederic Chassot (19, 64), Christophe Bonvin (23)</p>
<p>Attendance: 38,514</p>
<p>Liverpool win 8-4 on aggregate  </p>
<p>In Eindhoven: PSV Eindhoven (Netherlands) 2 Brann Bergen (Norway) 2 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>PSV - Rene Eykelkamp (74), Boudewijn Zenden (83)</p>
<p>Brann - Geir Hausund (35), Tore Andre Flo (59)</p>
<p>Attendance: 19,000</p>
<p>Brann win 4-3 on aggregate  </p>
<p>In Paris: Paris St Germain (France) 4 Galatasaray (Turkey) 0 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Leonardo (9), Julio Cesar Dely Valdes (22), Patrice Loko (58), Rai (78)</p>
<p>Attendance: 34,032</p>
<p>Paris win 6-4 on aggregate  </p>
<p>In Prague: Sparta Prague (Czech Republic) 1 Fiorentina (Italy) 1 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Sparta Prague - Vratislav Lokvenc (5)</p>
<p>Fiorentina - Anselmo Robbiati (63)</p>
<p>Attendance: 16,021</p>
<p>Fiorentina win 3-2 on aggregate.  </p>
<p>In Athens: AEK Athens (Greece) 4 Olimpija Ljubljana (Slovenia) 0 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Tony Saveski (4), Daniel Batista (34), Christos Maladenis (80), Christos Kostis (86)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>AEK win 6-0 on aggregate.</p>
</text>
